  "finding_closure": [
    "Actual fixed WGSL clean now returns zero for nonfinite or alpha<=0 data. This single production condition applies before current early return, neighborhood extrema, history accumulation and final output.",
    "Both scalar references use matching canonical clearing. New CPU controls distinguish malformed current, history-only and neighborhood-clamp contamination in both projections, with zero/negative-zero/negative alpha cases.",
    "The ignored actual shader case has residual [4,3,2,0] current/history plus dark opaque history. It checks exact zero at the clear edge and the 0.325 neighbor result, detecting residual-color contamination rather than merely repeating requested writes.",
    "Only the Resolve trusted source hash changes with the corrected program. Fixed 64-byte frame, texture/resource bindings, other program hashes and backend ABI remain unchanged."
  ],
  "reviewed_contracts": [
    "Current opaque invalid owner motion refuses history. Previous UV minus current UV uses top-left normalized coordinates and viewport extent; expected previous NDC depth converts to previous view distance correctly for both projections. Projection identity changes invalidate history.",
    "Positive inside-viewport bilinear taps are admitted individually and renormalized, no zero-mass divide or outside clamping. Nonfinite/negative history, invalid depths and invalid alpha are excluded or canonicalized as specified.",
    "A bounded 3x3 current neighborhood provides conservative depth-range support and nearest valid expected-depth motion, with stable center priority on ties. Range admission is a one-pixel silhouette policy, not exact object correspondence.",
    "Pure clear support lies near the far plane; even near-far foreground admitted by the numeric tolerance is clamped to zero by canonical all-clear neighborhood extrema. Covered background beyond the one-pixel neighborhood cannot retain foreground outside its current range/clamp.",
    "Premultiplied RGBA coverage is blended as a convex combination, including fractional/zero coverage. Reactive RGB reduction and existing configuration/defaults are unchanged.",
    "Test-only controlled post-MASK occupancy is honestly separated from real model/MASK rasterization. Independent f64 fixtures cover both projections, clear/depth edges, moving/trailing rejection, tie behavior, and malformed clear; they do not claim general full-raster or universal malformed-input equivalence."
  ],
